# Toolchain pins, read by CI and tests/stunt_lib.sh. Evidence-based, as in the
# rest of the Aether family: AE_PIN is the oldest ae this repository is
# verified against, bumped only in the commit that needs something newer.
#
# 0.875.0: the release current when the repository was set up (2026-11-04),
# and the one its tests were first run on (macOS arm64, Linux x86_64). Older
# releases were not tried. The bridge needs a release whose tarball ships
# include/aether/runtime (aether_sandbox.h) and, on Linux,
# lib/libaether_sandbox.so: both are in 0.875.0.
AE_PIN=0.875.0
# aeb is not used to build anything here yet; get.sh installs it with ae.
AEB_REF=v0.340
# The aether source ref stunt's catalogue is built from (stunt.c, stunt.h,
# stunt_main.c). Release tarballs ship contrib/host/stunt without stunt.c and
# stunt_main.c, so the catalogue comes from the source at the release's tag.
AETHER_STUNT_REF=v0.875.0
# The oldest ae with std.guest (the contained child's protocol, aether #3555):
# 0.878.0, the first published release that contains it. 0.876.0 and 0.877.0
# were tagged but never published (no binary assets).
AE_CHILD_PIN=0.878.0
# The oldest ae whose sandbox preload holds every libc way of starting a
# program (aether #3580): posix_spawn, system and popen included, so Lua's
# os.execute and io.popen follow the exec and fork grants in-process, and the
# contained child's own lockdown (no grants) refuses them. Below it they
# escape the preload. 0.884.0 is the first release with #3580. Not a floor:
# tests/stunt_lib.sh expects one or the other side of it from the ae it runs.
AE_SPAWN_PIN=0.884.0
